Based on OpenAI's skill design patterns article, this PR improves skill
descriptions to help agents route more accurately:

1. Added 'Use when / Don't use when' format to all descriptions
2. Added explicit negative examples to prevent misfires
3. Added overlap clarification tables for related tools
4. Kept descriptions concise (routing logic, not marketing)

Skills updated:
- peekaboo: clarified native apps vs browser/CLI
- nano-banana-pro: distinguished generation from analysis
- gemini: explained cost optimization use case
- github: separated platform ops from code work
- 1password: added security rules
- coding-agent: clarified delegation vs direct edits
- weather: added data limitations
- clawhub: distinguished from skill-creator
- apple-notes: added ecosystem constraints
- blogwatcher: added RSS-only limitation
- healthcheck: added access safety warning
- nano-pdf: clarified edit vs create
- skill-creator: distinguished from clawhub
