+- **Issues**: Create, list, comment, close, label
+- **Releases**: Create releases, list tags
+- **API queries**: Access any GitHub API endpoint with `gh api`
+- **Quick lookups**: "Is CI passing?", "What PRs are open?", "Who's assigned to this issue?"
+
+## When NOT to Use
+
+- **Code review**: Use `coding-agent` — it can actually read and analyze the code
+- **Code changes**: Use `git` for commits, `coding-agent` for writing code
+- **Visual browsing**: For exploring unfamiliar repos, browser might be easier
+- **Unauthenticated**: Check `gh auth status` first — most commands need auth
+- **Repo settings**: Branch protection, webhooks, etc. — web UI is clearer
+- **Complex code search**: GitHub's code search in browser is more powerful
