 # Nano Banana Pro (Gemini 3 Pro Image)
 
+Generate and edit images using Google's Gemini 3 Pro Image model.
+
+## When to Use
+
+- **Image generation**: Create images from text descriptions ("a sunset over mountains")
+- **Image editing**: Modify existing images ("make the sky more dramatic", "add a person walking")
+- **Multi-image composition**: Combine up to 14 images into a single scene
+- **Visual content creation**: Blog headers, social media graphics, concept art
+
+## When NOT to Use
+
+- **Image analysis**: If you need to understand/describe what's in an image, use the `image` tool instead
+- **Screenshots**: Use Peekaboo (macOS apps) or browser tool (web pages)
+- **Diagrams/charts/graphs**: Use code generation (matplotlib, mermaid, d3.js) — more precise and editable
+- **Text-heavy images**: AI image generators are bad at rendering text accurately
+- **Pixel-perfect design**: Use proper design tools (Figma, Canva) for precise work
+- **Logos/brand assets**: Usually need a human designer for brand consistency
+
+## Overlap Clarification
+
+| Task | Use This | Why |
+|------|----------|-----|
+| "What's in this image?" | `image` tool | Analysis, not generation |
+| "Create a landscape painting" | **nano-banana-pro** ✓ | Generation from prompt |
+| "Add a hat to this photo" | **nano-banana-pro** ✓ | Image editing |
+| "Screenshot this website" | `browser` tool | Capture, not generate |
+| "Make a flowchart" | Code (mermaid) | Precise, editable, text-accurate |
+
+## Limitations
+
+- **Text in images**: Often garbled or misspelled — avoid prompts requiring readable text
+- **Specific styles**: Results vary; may need prompt iteration
+- **Content policy**: Some subjects (violence, certain people) may be restricted
+- **Faces**: Quality can be inconsistent; may hit safety filters
+
+---
+
 Use the bundled script to generate or edit images.
 
