 # Peekaboo
 
-Peekaboo is a full macOS UI automation CLI: capture/inspect screens, target UI
-elements, drive input, and manage apps/windows/menus. Commands share a snapshot
-cache and support `--json`/`-j` for scripting. Run `peekaboo` or
-`peekaboo <cmd> --help` for flags; `peekaboo --version` prints build metadata.
-Tip: run via `polter peekaboo` to ensure fresh builds.
+Automate native macOS applications through accessibility APIs when no CLI/API exists.
+
+## When to Use
+
+- **Native app automation**: Click buttons, fill forms, navigate menus in apps like System Settings, Finder, Mail, Notes
+- **Screen inspection**: Take annotated screenshots (`see --annotate`) to identify clickable elements before acting
+- **Window management**: Resize, move, focus, minimize windows programmatically
+- **Menu bar / Dock**: Click status bar items, launch apps from Dock, access app menus
+- **No programmatic access**: The app doesn't expose a CLI, API, or AppleScript dictionary
+
+## When NOT to Use
+
+- **Web pages**: Use the `browser` tool instead — it has DOM access and more reliable selectors
+- **Apps with CLIs**: If the app has a CLI (e.g., `gh` for GitHub, `code` for VS Code), use that — more reliable and scriptable
+- **Apps with APIs**: Direct API calls beat UI automation every time
+- **File operations**: Use shell commands (`exec`), not UI clicks
+- **Simple app launching**: Just use `open -a "App Name"` — simpler and faster
+- **Non-macOS**: Peekaboo only works on macOS (uses Accessibility framework)
+- **Missing permissions**: Requires Screen Recording + Accessibility permissions — check with `peekaboo permissions`
+
+## Overlap Clarification
+
+| Task | Use This | Not Peekaboo Because |
+|------|----------|---------------------|
+| Click button on website | `browser` tool | Browser has DOM selectors, more reliable |
+| Open GitHub PR | `gh pr view` | CLI is scriptable, works headless |
+| Launch Safari | `open -a Safari` | Simpler, no accessibility needed |
+| Click "Allow" in System Settings | **Peekaboo** ✓ | No CLI for this, must use UI |
+| Resize Finder window | **Peekaboo** ✓ | Window management is a strength |
+| Read text from a PDF | `exec` with `pdftotext` | CLI tool is more reliable |
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+- macOS only
+- Screen Recording permission (for screenshots/see)
+- Accessibility permission (for clicking/typing)
+- Check status: `peekaboo permissions`
+
+---
+
+Commands share a snapshot cache and support `--json`/`-j` for scripting. Run `peekaboo` or `peekaboo <cmd> --help` for flags.
 
